DELETE FROM kb_planet_in_sign WHERE planet = 'South Node';

INSERT INTO kb_planet_in_sign (planet, sign, summary, life_patterns, relationships, challenges, growth, book_references) VALUES
('South Node', 'Libra', 'You naturally understand partnership, diplomacy, and how to keep the peace. These gifts come easily because you''ve done this for many lifetimes. But your comfort zone has become your cage—you lose yourself in relationships, avoid necessary conflict, and abandon your own needs to maintain harmony. You''re here to learn the opposite.', 'You immediately see all sides of every situation. You''re a natural peacekeeper who smooths conflicts before they begin. People rely on you for balance and fairness. But your comfort with compromise keeps you stuck in situations where you accept too little for yourself. You''re learning when not to compromise.', 'Partnership feels natural and necessary—perhaps too natural. You can disappear entirely into a relationship, losing your own preferences and desires. You''re attracted to partners who need your balance. The work is learning to have boundaries and preferences that matter as much as harmony does.', 'You''ll sacrifice almost anything to keep the peace. Your own needs feel less important than maintaining balance. You struggle to voice disagreement or anger. People-pleasing is so automatic that you don''t realize you''re doing it. You feel guilty when you choose yourself over someone else.', 'Your growth comes from learning that true balance requires you to take up space. The peace you maintain must include your own truth. Relationships deepen when you stop being the eternal mediator and become a real person with needs. Authentic relating replaces performed harmony.', ARRAY['Schulman, Karmic Astrology: The Moon''s Nodes and Reincarnation']),

('South Node', 'Scorpio', 'You naturally understand depth, transformation, and the hidden aspects of psychology. These gifts come easily because you''ve spent many lifetimes in intensity and darkness. But now your comfort with crisis, control, and emotional extremes is keeping you stuck. You''re here to learn stability, trust, and the value of what''s ordinary and real.', 'You''re drawn to complexity, mystery, and transformation. You understand power dynamics intuitively. You''re comfortable with intensity and darkness that others avoid. But your attraction to chaos keeps you in turbulent relationships and situations. You''re learning that peace, not crisis, is the real teacher.', 'You need deep connection and complete honesty—nothing superficial will do. You can love intensely but your relationships often involve power struggles or crisis. Partners feel the weight of your need for transformation and control. Your growth involves learning that real love allows things to simply be.', 'You seek transformation constantly, even when stability would serve you better. You distrust ease and comfort, believing real depth requires struggle. You can be manipulative in relationships, using psychological insights as weapons. Simple happiness feels boring and untrustworthy.', 'Your growth comes from learning that boring stability is actually precious. Real power lies in building something that lasts, not in control or crisis. Relationships heal when you stop trying to transform others and accept them. Trust and simplicity become your unexpected gifts.', ARRAY['Schulman, Karmic Astrology: The Moon''s Nodes and Reincarnation']),

('South Node', 'Sagittarius', 'You naturally understand belief, philosophy, and the bigger picture. These gifts come easily because you''ve spent lifetimes gathering wisdom. But your comfort with certainty, preaching, and grand ideas is keeping you stuck. You''re here to learn to listen, gather information, and honor what you don''t know. Your authority is your cage.', 'You see the truth from your perspective and have no doubt about it. You''re comfortable teaching, preaching, and speaking with authority. You gather knowledge and enthusiastically share what you''ve learned. But you stop listening once you''ve decided what''s true. Life keeps trying to teach you humility.', 'You need others to agree with your vision and adopt your philosophy. Relationships feel like teaching opportunities where you help others see the truth. You get frustrated when partners don''t understand or adopt your perspective. Your growth involves genuine curiosity about how they think.', 'You know too much and listen too little. Your certainty shuts down real dialogue. You can be righteously judgmental about people who don''t share your beliefs. Admitting you were wrong or don''t have the full picture feels impossible. Your need to be right isolates you.', 'Your growth comes from genuine intellectual humility. Real wisdom includes admitting what you don''t know. Relationships deepen when you ask real questions instead of delivering truth. Your influence grows when you listen first. Knowledge without wisdom is your karmic lesson.', ARRAY['Schulman, Karmic Astrology: The Moon''s Nodes and Reincarnation']),

('South Node', 'Gemini', 'You naturally gather information, communicate, and see from multiple angles. These gifts come easily because you''ve spent many lifetimes in intellectual exchange. But your comfort with surface knowledge, talking, and analysis is keeping you stuck. You''re here to learn depth, conviction, and the power of your own truth. Information is your cage.', 'You''re drawn to learning, conversation, and movement. You pick up information easily and enjoy explaining it to others. You see multiple perspectives and can argue any side. But you rarely commit to anything deep. You''re learning to stop gathering and start synthesizing. Life keeps pushing you toward conviction.', 'You''re curious about how people think but can remain emotionally distant. Relationships need you to go deeper, but you often stay in pleasant conversation. Partners feel like they don''t fully have you. Your growth involves commitment and emotional truth over intellectual exchange.', 'You get bored easily and skip things before they get deep. Your knowledge is broad but shallow. You talk more than you listen and move on before understanding. The commitment and depth required for real intimacy feel limiting. You rationalize away your emotions.', 'Your growth comes from developing real conviction and depth. Wisdom replaces information. Relationships deepen when you stay present with difficult emotions instead of talking around them. Your real power emerges when you integrate what you''ve learned. Commitment becomes your superpower.', ARRAY['Schulman, Karmic Astrology: The Moon''s Nodes and Reincarnation']),

('South Node', 'Capricorn', 'You naturally understand authority, structure, and how to build something real. These gifts come easily because you''ve spent lifetimes creating order and achievement. But your comfort with control, responsibility, and achievement is keeping you stuck. You''re here to learn vulnerability, emotional truth, and the courage to show up as a whole person. Your power is your cage.', 'You''re drawn to leadership, building, and creating lasting structures. You understand responsibility and follow through. You accomplish things others don''t. But you''ve built a carefully controlled life that leaves little room for spontaneous emotion or vulnerability. Life keeps inviting you to feel.', 'You''re reliable and capable but can be distant emotionally. Relationships need your presence, not just your provision. Partners feel like they''re managing the emotional work while you manage everything else. Your growth involves letting down your guard and showing that you need people too.', 'You''re uncomfortable with emotional expression and dependency. Vulnerability feels like weakness. You control situations through competence rather than connection. The softness required for real intimacy feels dangerous. You often prioritize achievement over relationships.', 'Your growth comes from learning that leadership includes emotional availability. Real power includes admitting you need people. Relationships flourish when you let others matter more than your goals. Your vulnerability becomes your greatest strength. Heart before ambition is your lesson.', ARRAY['Schulman, Karmic Astrology: The Moon''s Nodes and Reincarnation']),

('South Node', 'Cancer', 'You naturally understand family, emotional safety, and what it means to care for others. These gifts come easily because you''ve spent lifetimes nurturing and maintaining the home. But your comfort with caregiving, safety, and family is keeping you stuck. You''re here to learn independence, courage, and that your own desires matter as much as others'' needs. Your refuge is your cage.', 'You''re drawn to family, home, and creating emotional safety. You sense what others need and naturally provide it. You''re comfortable with routine, tradition, and the familiar. But you''ve made yourself so necessary that you''ve forgotten who you are apart from caring for others. Life keeps asking you to claim your own space.', 'You''re nurturing and present but can suffocate others with your care. Relationships need your independence, not just your emotional presence. Partners feel responsible for your feelings. Your growth involves developing your own interests and needs that exist apart from family.', 'You cling to family and familiar situations even when they''re unhealthy. The independence required to pursue your own dreams feels selfish. You use caregiving as a way to maintain control. Your fear of being alone keeps you in comfortable but stunted situations.', 'Your growth comes from learning that honoring yourself honors those you love. You''re learning that independence and care aren''t opposites. Real love includes letting others become what they need to be. Your courage to pursue your own life is what allows others to pursue theirs.', ARRAY['Schulman, Karmic Astrology: The Moon''s Nodes and Reincarnation']),

('South Node', 'Aquarius', 'You naturally understand the collective, ideals, and how to remain detached. These gifts come easily because you''ve spent lifetimes serving movements or ideas. But your comfort with groups, detachment, and ideas is keeping you stuck. You''re here to learn individuality, creative self-expression, and that your personal gifts matter. Your idealism is your cage.', 'You''re drawn to groups, causes, and ideas that serve the collective. You''re comfortable being part of something bigger. You see humanity as a whole and work for the greater good. But you''ve lost your own voice and presence. Your individuality feels irrelevant. Life keeps asking you to shine personally.', 'You relate through shared ideals but can remain emotionally distant. Relationships need your personal presence and expression, not just your agreement with their ideals. Partners feel you retreating into the group or the cause. Your growth involves being visible as a unique person.', 'You hide in groups to avoid standing out. Your own creative gifts feel less important than collective work. Personal achievement feels selfish. You''re uncomfortable with attention or being special. Your detachment protects you from genuine intimacy.', 'Your growth comes from learning that your unique gifts serve the whole. Real power is visible and personal before it becomes collective. Relationships deepen when you show your actual self. Your individuality is your contribution. Leadership comes through expressing who you are.', ARRAY['Schulman, Karmic Astrology: The Moon''s Nodes and Reincarnation']),

('South Node', 'Leo', 'You naturally understand self-expression, creativity, and how to shine. These gifts come easily because you''ve spent lifetimes in the spotlight. But your comfort with being the center, needing admiration, and personal glory is keeping you stuck. You''re here to learn to serve others, share the stage, and find meaning beyond personal recognition. Your light is your cage.', 'You''re drawn to visibility, creativity, and being the center of attention. You understand how to command a room and love being special. You''re generous with your gifts but always aware of how well you''re performing. But your need for recognition keeps you from real intimacy and service.', 'You need admiration and can resent others'' success. Relationships are partly an audience for your performance. Partners feel your need for them to see how special you are. Your growth involves loving others without needing them to verify your worth.', 'Your ego is invested in being the best or most important. You struggle when attention goes elsewhere. The humility required to serve without recognition feels like erasure. You need to be special, which prevents you from being genuinely intimate.', 'Your growth comes from learning that real power serves, not dominates. Your gifts multiply when shared freely without the need for credit. Relationships deepen when you can be genuinely interested in others'' shining. Your greatest creativity flows when it''s not about proving anything.', ARRAY['Schulman, Karmic Astrology: The Moon''s Nodes and Reincarnation']),

('South Node', 'Virgo', 'You naturally understand service, detail, and how to perfect systems. These gifts come easily because you''ve spent lifetimes in dedicated craft. But your comfort with criticism, perfectionism, and control through analysis is keeping you stuck. You''re here to learn to surrender, embrace mystery, and that good enough is perfect. Your precision is your cage.', 'You''re drawn to perfecting things, organizing systems, and serving through detailed work. You see what''s wrong and naturally fix it. You''re reliable and competent. But your eye for detail becomes critical judgment. You''re learning to let things be imperfect and trust the bigger picture.', 'You can be critical of yourself and others. Relationships need your acceptance, not your improvements. Partners feel analyzed and found wanting. Your growth involves loving people and situations as they are, not as you''d like to improve them.', 'You can''t let things be imperfect. The mess and chaos of life feel unbearable. You use criticism as a way to feel in control. Surrendering to mystery or accepting good-enough feels like failure. Your perfectionism isolates you and prevents real spontaneity.', 'Your growth comes from learning that surrender is not failure. Life has a wisdom that transcends your analysis. Compassion replaces criticism. Relationships flourish when you accept people completely. Your real service is being present, not perfecting everything.', ARRAY['Schulman, Karmic Astrology: The Moon''s Nodes and Reincarnation']),

('South Node', 'Pisces', 'You naturally understand compassion, spirituality, and transcendence. These gifts come easily because you''ve spent lifetimes in mystical practice. But your comfort with escape, merging with others, and avoiding the practical world is keeping you stuck. You''re here to learn to show up fully in reality and perfect your craft. Your spirituality is your cage.', 'You''re drawn to spirituality, mysticism, and anything that offers escape from ordinary reality. You can easily merge with others'' emotions. You''re intuitive and compassionate. But you use spirituality to avoid the mundane work. You''re learning that the sacred lives in detail and discipline.', 'You can lose yourself in relationships or rescuing others. Relationships need your clear boundaries and practical presence. Partners feel you''re not fully here. Your growth involves being reliably present, not just spiritually connected.', 'You escape into spirituality or fantasy when reality feels hard. Your boundaries are unclear and you take on others'' emotions. The discipline and detail required for real mastery feels tedious. You often underachieve because you''re not committed to the practical world.', 'Your growth comes from learning that spirituality is embodied in disciplined work. Real compassion requires clear boundaries and practical service. Mastery comes through daily practice, not inspiration. Your greatest gifts emerge when you show up fully in the world.', ARRAY['Schulman, Karmic Astrology: The Moon''s Nodes and Reincarnation']),

('South Node', 'Aries', 'You naturally understand independence, courage, and how to go it alone. These gifts come easily because you''ve spent lifetimes pioneering and asserting yourself. But your comfort with conflict, separation, and doing things alone is keeping you stuck. You''re here to learn partnership, compromise, and that real strength includes receiving from others. Your autonomy is your cage.', 'You''re drawn to independent action and making your own way. You''re courageous and don''t hesitate to pioneer. You''re comfortable with conflict and confrontation. But your independence keeps you isolated. Life keeps inviting you into partnership. You''re learning that true strength includes interdependence.', 'You can be combative or quick to anger in relationships. Partnerships feel like loss of freedom. You resist anyone''s influence or suggestions. Partners feel you don''t need them. Your growth involves genuine collaboration where two people create something neither could alone.', 'You''re stubborn and resistant to compromise. Your way feels right and others'' ways feel wrong. The vulnerability required to truly need someone feels like weakness. You often end up alone because you won''t meet others halfway.', 'Your growth comes from learning that partnership is not submission. Real courage includes acknowledging others'' worth equally with your own. Relationships deepen when you can truly listen and adjust your course. Your independence becomes real freedom when it includes genuine connection.', ARRAY['Schulman, Karmic Astrology: The Moon''s Nodes and Reincarnation']),

('South Node', 'Taurus', 'You naturally understand stability, beauty, and the sensory world. These gifts come easily because you''ve spent lifetimes building and enjoying what endures. But your comfort with accumulation, resistance to change, and attachment to what''s familiar is keeping you stuck. You''re here to learn transformation, letting go, and that the only constant is change. Your stability is your cage.', 'You''re drawn to building, collecting, and creating stability. You appreciate sensory pleasures and physical comfort. You''re reliable and grounded. But you resist necessary change and hold on too long to what''s familiar. Life keeps taking things away to teach you about impermanence.', 'You need security and can feel threatened by your partner''s growth or change. Relationships need your willingness to evolve. Partners feel you''re stuck in familiar patterns. Your growth involves embracing transformation even when it feels destabilizing.', 'You fear change and loss. Material security feels essential. You hold on to relationships, jobs, or situations long after they''ve stopped serving you. The letting go required for real growth feels like death. You use comfort as a buffer against life''s intensity.', 'Your growth comes from learning that security lies in your ability to adapt, not in what you own. Release becomes your superpower. Relationships deepen when you can change together. Your real strength emerges when you can let go of what no longer serves.', ARRAY['Schulman, Karmic Astrology: The Moon''s Nodes and Reincarnation']);
